  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 is the most Northwind-favourable term: the 5% limit has no sales stop, the corrective period has no fixed end, existing models are not exempt, and per-model results go to purchasers and regulators but not the public, which protects the Hearth 10 at 6.2%. S5 imposes an 8-per-100k mandatory recall with no transition and immediate notice, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while S3's six-year retrofit window favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage. S4's 36-month suppression start is the within-range term Halcyon required, and S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all incidents, which both companies' unreported incidents fall under."
 },
